## Database setup

The application reads the database URL from the `DATABASE_URL` environment
variable. The generated default is:

```text
{{ spec.database_url }}
```
{% if spec.has("postgres") %}

With PostgreSQL selected, the default points at the `db` service described in
`docker-compose.yml`. Set `DATABASE_URL` in `.env` to use a different database.
{% else %}

SQLite is used by default and the database file is created on first use.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

## Test

```sh
uv run pytest
```
{% if spec.has("sqlalchemy") %}

Database tests override `DATABASE_URL` with a temporary SQLite file, so they run
without a PostgreSQL server even when PostgreSQL is selected.
